Section~\ref{sec:fake_safety} establishes that fake safety dominates Pi0's CAR scores. A natural question remains: could a perfect SDF signal enable effective refinement? We test this with oracle experiments (Section~\ref{sec:oracle_setup}) that replace the learned SDF with ground-truth distance fields from simulation geometry. If EE-only refinement is structurally sound, these oracles should exceed unrefined baselines by a wide margin.

